WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.920
(Background city noise)

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:16.260
(Laughing)

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.660
Hello Internet, Welcome to Film Theory

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.500
a show that DARES to ask:

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.480
just because Jellicles can and Jellicles do

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.540
does that mean Jellicles should???

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.980
THAT’S RIGHT theater kids

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.700
put down your copy of "Noises off"

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.080
and hit PAUSE on that "Dear Evan Hansen" playlist

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.860
because TODAY we're talking about the

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.860
movie that horrified the world.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.560
Or at least would've horrified the world

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.100
if anyone had actually gone to see it.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.040
(Haha it did bad)

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:39.800
CATS!!!

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.080
The Musical Extravaganza!

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.280
See I put an exclamation point there

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.020
because all the good musicals have to have to end

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.640
end their title with an exclamation point.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.140
Thirsty cats, ~thirsty~ cats if you know what i'm saying...

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.140
Rebel Wilson, unzipping off her skin...

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.940
Judy Dench, sniffing butts...

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.360
Cats is a movie experience,

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.980
that truly has something for

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.260
everyone.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.600
Prompting all sorts of glowing reviews,

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:06.100
such as the Boston Globe's: "My eyes are burning. Oh God, my eyes."

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.900
The Beat's: "Cats is the worst thing to happen to cats since dogs."

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:15.200
and Collider's astute observation: "Can you make a movie so bad that the Academy takes back your Best Director Oscar?"

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:21.000
Then, of course, you have my review which is that Cats is the most I have laughed at a movie in years.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.460
"Laughed at" being the operative words there.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.260
This thing starts weird,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:28.400
and just as your mind is starting to come to grips of what you're seeing

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.180
it just ratchets the weird up in the very next scene.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.280
Didn't also help that I was in a theatre full of people meowing at the screen

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.440
and also next to a girl who kept asking "Where's Taylor?!"

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:41.460
This thing is like the new family friendly "Rocky Horror Picture Show."

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.620
Fewer corsets, more hairballs. *bArFiNG*

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.340
Or you know, maybe I am going in too soon by calling it family-friendly

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.220
because that doesn't seem to be the right word.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:53.560
"Cats!" Has a dark, sinister underbelly to it.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:57.040
If you try and put your finger on it, well it just scratches back.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.340
True to its name-sake.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:05.120
So today we are diving deep into this uncanny valley to answer the age-old question, "What is a Jellicle cat?"

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:11.380
And the response hiding behind those CGI whiskers is that Jellicle cats may better be described as a Jellicle Cult.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:16.580
A group of brainwashed indoctrinated cats lied to by a charismatic leader

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.400
only to be ritualistically sacrificed.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.840
This isn't even a joke.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:26.340
So today let's talk about the 4 billion dollar  musical that, like toxoplasmosis gondii,

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.720
brainwashed all us humans into being mindless slaves to our clawed little companions.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:32.700
Let's look at the facts

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.700
According to Michael Bluejay, an ex-member of the real life New York City cult,  Aesthetic Realism,

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:42.600
cults use an 8-step framework in order to recruit and indoctrinate their new members.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.160
And those 8 steps map shockingly well onto all the events

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.800
that we see taking place throughout the runtime of Cats.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.120
First though, before we indoctrinate anyone, we have to pick our target.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:55.280
While there are countless examples showing that anyone can fall prey

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.660
to a charismatic leader with a convincing message,

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:01.360
research has shown that people who are the most susceptible to cult recruitment

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.500
are stressed, emotionally vulnerable, have tenuous or no family connections,

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.060
and are often living in poor socioeconomic conditions.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.820
And that makes a lot of sense, right?

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.340
A confident, well-to-do person with a lot of love in their life

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.300
is gonna have a stronger sense of identity

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.140
than someone who's struggling to get by.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:19.740
Humans are prone to rush to those with open arms and rational solutions.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.580
Apparently the same is true for cats.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:25.400
The movie opens and we're immediately introduced to Victoria,

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.400
a wide-eyed, curious young kitten,

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.300
shoved into a sack and abandoned in an alleyway by her human owners.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:34.080
Let's say that getting dumped at night in a brand new part of town

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.720
might inspire some feelings of stress and vulnerability.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.620
Even her song, Beautiful Ghosts, is all about feelings of

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.040
longing, loneliness, and a need for validation.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.980
One look at the lyrics tells you everything you need to know.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:47.260
Quote, "All that I wanted was to be wanted"

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.620
"too young to wander London streets alone and haunted"

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.780
"born into nothing, at least YOU have something"

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:54.940
"something to cling to"

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:58.180
"visions of dazzling rooms I'll never get let into."

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:02.120
Victoria, quite simply, is the perfect target for a cult.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.920
Wouldn't you know it, but the Jellicles are there to greet her with open arms.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.800
Open... CGI hand-paw... things?

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.560
These cats have weird unique names that make them special and different,

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.820
and part of something bigger than themselves.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.880
We're told that each cat has themselves 3 names:

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:22.420
their human-given name, their Jellicle name, and their unspoken secret identity name.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:25.360
And those names are an important detail here.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:28.300
One thing that former cult members talk a lot about

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:32.120
is how a cult manages to separate it's new members from their former identities.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.300
Cults encourage cutting off any ties to the past,

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.700
and that often includes cutting off ties to birth names.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:41.700
A perfect example of this is the Manson family cult,

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:45.060
where individuals identify themselves like "Tex" and "Gypsy".

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.460
These were new names,

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.820
nicknames that were bestowed and used by the cult members.

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:52.180
So, from the start of Cats the movie,

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:55.180
the Jellicle cats are exhibiting classic cult behavior.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.180
And that's without me even mentioning the fact that

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.480
all this naming stuff was told to her in a chant,

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.780
like a creed, in that opening song.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:05.180
So with our innocent, naive Victoria as a mark all picked out,

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.000
it's time to walk her through the steps.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.080
Step 1: inviting her to a non-threatening event,

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.880
something that's easy to say "yes" to because it requires a low level of commitment.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.920
Now, this first step can take many forms:

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:19.260
meeting, informational-gathering, a get-together,

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.160
a party, a gala, a ball.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:24.180
Ahahaha... the Jellicle ball,

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.720
where all the cats get together to just, you know,

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.900
have a night of fun singing, dancing,

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.600
ultimately sacrificing one of their members...

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.600
BUT! Well, we're not gonna talk about THAT yet,

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.720
that's later in the evening.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:38.340
Let's just invite Victoria to the party for now and have some fun, drink some milk,

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:42.080
go watch the... hip hop cats in their little tennis shoes... perform.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.620
After agreeing to attend, Victoria starts meeting a lot of new faces,

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:48.980
and starts getting herself a LOT of positive attention,

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:51.220
especially from all the males in the Jellicle group.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:54.640
But of them all, it's Rum Tum Tugger who stands out the most.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:57.680
You see, his song makes it clear that he's the hot one.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.960
He is seductive, he is the good singer and heck,

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.980
he's even got himself backup dancers who wear tennis shoes.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:03.960
And what do you know?

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.120
In a lineup of cats thirsty for all of that milk of his,

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:09.840
his... little milk 'cause they're dancing at a milk bar,

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.160
he picks Victoria out from the crowd.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:17.120
This is the perfect example of Step 2 in the indoctrination process: love bombing.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:20.340
This is when cult members shower potential victims with praise and attention

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:24.340
in the hopes of creating a positive association between the cult and good feelings.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:28.020
This makes people, or apparently felines, wanna show up for more

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.260
and deepen their relationship with these groups

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:33.000
OR with specific members of these groups.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.640
Step 3: dangling the prize.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.580
Now, all these cats have presumably followed Bob Barker's advice

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.220
and gotten themselves spayed and neutered,

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:42.860
so nothing should literally be "dangling" here.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.760
Instead, the prize that the Jellicle cats care about

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.440
is the "Jellicle Choice".

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:51.780
The cats explain that Old Deuteronomy, a wise cat who's lived herself 99 lives,

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:54.760
who is a cookie cutter example of a cult leader by the way,

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.600
will choose 1 cat to ascend to a higher plane of existence.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.740
Or get reborn or whatever, the details don't matter to us viewers

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.740
or quite honestly, to the cats either.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:06.020
They're already drinking the Kool-Aid here,

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:09.320
except this time "drinking the Kool-Aid" means "drinking the milk".

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:11.980
Anyway! The Heaviside layer is the prize that goes to

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:15.280
the one good deserving Jellicle each and every year.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.160
It sounds completely insane right?

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.660
Especially when you start to pick apart what the promise actually means.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:22.820
You get reborn into a better life, but

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:25.660
you don't get to keep any memories of your former life?

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:28.720
And yet Old Deuteronomy claims to have lived 99 lives

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:31.720
So did she ascend? Did she keep her memories?

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.960
The claims just don't really add up,

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:36.280
but unfortunately, this is what cults do.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:38.360
They dangle an attractive prize

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:42.140
and because you're suddenly in a safe space full of love and people that care about you,

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.520
the cult has created this bubble around you

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.260
one full of love and acceptance.

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:49.300
Opportunities like the Heaviside Layer and the Jellicle Choice

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:52.060
seem totally reasonable, totally possible

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:55.040
something that you absolutely wanna have for yourself.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:58.240
We see real life cults doing stuff like this time and time again

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:01.260
through tragedies such as Jonestown and Heaven's Gate

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:04.780
In both of these cases, members were pushed to sacrifice themselves

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:09.040
as a way to "ascend", or reach the next step in their evolutionary process.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:11.580
Even the language that they use is remarkably similar to

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:14.540
how the Heaviside Layer is described in the lyrics of Cats.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:17.620
The Heaven's Gate cult rallied around the following message, quote:

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:20.600
"The comet brings closure to Heaven's Gate"

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:24.920
"Our 22 years of classroom here on planet Earth is finally coming to conclusion"

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:31.360
"Graduation from the human evolutionary level. We are happily prepared to leave this world." End quote.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.800
And then over in Jonestown, the night when members sacrificed themselves,

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.340
cult leader Jim Jones was recorded as telling members, quote again:

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:42.480
"If you knew what was ahead of you, you'd be glad to be stepping over tonight."

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:45.160
And all of these examples share one commonality -

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.840
the use of odd or specialized language.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:51.780
"Evolutionary levels", "stepping over", "Heaviside Layers", and "Jellicle Choices"

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:54.920
All of it is odd, specialized language.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:56.420
In both the movie and in real life,

00:08:56.420 --> 00:09:00.080
it's yet another tactic to reinforce an "us versus them" mindset.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.840
We see this in the final musical number of Cats,

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:07.120
when Old Deuteronomy lists off all the ways that a cat is different from a dog.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.540
Jellicle cats are different. They're special.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:11.860
This way of thinking supports the idea that

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:15.440
"we Jellicle cats understand things that others don't".

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:20.400
And it also means that when others criticize the cult and point out its dangerous flaws,

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:22.740
members can easily write all that stuff off,

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.200
because non-members "just don't get it."

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.260
Which, leads us to the end of the movie,

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:32.180
where Victoria is asked to complete Step 4, and perhaps the biggest step in the indoctrination process:

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:36.240
extracting an agreement from you that you want the prize.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.460
Old Deuteronomy singles Victoria out.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:42.680
She embraces her into the family and asks if she'd like to join the Jellicles,

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:45.280
even giving her her own Jellicle name.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:49.680
Victoria has met the members, is already romantically involved with at least one,

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:54.800
and has just finished watching her first ritualistic choice, and she says "YES".

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.520
She is now in deep.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:59.080
And from here on out, she's a Jellicle.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:01.720
A "Jellicle" is part of her identity now.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:03.640
She's enlisted into the cult.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:06.840
And while Victoria may complete the movie only having made it through Step 4,

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:11.440
we actually see the other 4 steps of this framework taking place throughout the rest of the evening.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:15.520
Step 5 is shutting down dissent with a threat to without the prize.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:18.800
This is in order to inspire good obedient behavior.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:21.680
And THAT is the essence of the Jellicle Choice.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.220
Only 1 member can win every year,

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:27.920
which means that everyone vies for the prize only to wind up rejected.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.480
It keeps that prize dangling tantalizingly close in front of their faces,

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.760
but always just out of their reach.

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:35.480
It keeps them wanting more.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.880
I mean, Macavity, this film's villain,

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:42.860
is simply a member of the Jellicles driven mad by how badly he wants to be the Jellicle Choice.

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:46.000
Consider this: Why do most of these cats want this prize to begin with?

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.000
Why do they want to be reborn?

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.780
Many of them explicitly sing about how good they currently have it.

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:54.260
Jennyanydots talks about how she sleeps all day

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:57.760
and finds joy teaching mice and roaches about Jellicle cats in the evening.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.520
In other words, she's evangelizing for the Jellicles,

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:02.680
spreading the word of the cult. But she is doing fine.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.500
Why would she want to be reborn?

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:07.680
Bustopher Jones meanwhile sings about how much he loves eating garbage.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.820
He is fat and happy like me after an all-you-can-eat buffet.

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.820
What's he got to complain about?

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.720
And then there's Skimbleshanks the railway cat

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:18.180
whose song tells stories of an exciting fulfilling life on the rails.

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:21.640
Why would any of these cats wanna die and start again?

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:24.840
It's because they believe that's what they're supposed to want.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:28.940
It's because they've been brainwashed by Old Deuteronomy's teachings.

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:32.780
Enter Grizabella, a cat that was once part of the Jellicle tribe,

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:34.800
but who's since been ousted from the group.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:38.420
Through Grizabella we see what happens when someone strays.

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:41.100
Heh get it? "Stray"? You know, stray cat?

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:43.160
Anyway! The strayer is ostracized.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.760
Publicly ridiculed and isolated.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:48.900
Grizabella serves as a warning sign to the other cats.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:51.400
She's bad because she strayed from the group.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.980
Doubters bad. Believers good.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:57.520
Grizabella getting ostracized for doubting Old Deuteronomy and the Jellicles

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.520
serves as a warning sign for the others.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.660
"THIS could be you!"

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:04.100
Again, it's shutting down dissent.

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:07.560
It's meant to inspire feelings of fear in the minds of the other cats.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:11.860
Fear and guilt about any inclinations they might have to doubt the Jellicle life.

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.920
But to Grizabella, it actually serves a different purpose,

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:19.660
and that is Step 6 of the indoctrination process: establishment of guilt.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:24.040
The leader shames recruits, which in turn makes them vulnerable to further manipulation.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:27.380
Grizabella is humiliated, knocking her ego down,

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:32.260
which brings her literally crawling back to the Jellicles for her new chance at life.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:36.740
And all of this relates to Step 7, what Bluejay calls "the carrot and the stick".

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:39.260
when the cult leader, in this case Old Deuteronomy,

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:43.240
rewards the cats for their good behavior, and punishes the cats for the bad behavior.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:46.220
Again, we see this in the final scene with Victoria.

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:48.220
She is given a name, she's given praise,

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:51.540
she's given high status next to leader on the Jellicle statue.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:55.320
As well as with Grizabella, who's rewarded for being repented.

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:58.840
She regrets her decision to doubt the Jellicles and comes back to the fold.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:03.160
And thanks to her good work, she's rewarded as that year's Jellicle Choice.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:06.540
Which leads us to the 8th and final step in this process

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:09.160
something we see hints at many times throughout the film:

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:12.340
control of identity, information, and environment.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:15.540
By naming them Jellicle cats, the way the cats literally sing a song

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:18.880
that lists what lists off all the things a Jellicle cat should and shouldn't be

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:20.460
is how they control identity.

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:23.900
The only source of information for Victoria in the film is other Jellicles.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:25.260
They could tell her anything they want.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:27.000
She has no means of fact-checking.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:30.380
And the environment is something that's also being run by the Jellicles.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.140
We see that in every song,

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:35.960
in which we discover there's a Jellicle cat for pretty much every building and location in the city,

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:39.540
whether it's the Milk Bar, the railroad, the fancy homes with lavish bedrooms.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.200
The Jellicles control it all.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:44.420
In the, it's clear that this cult has been successful.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:47.600
The Jellicle Choice is made, Grizabella is sent off to ascend.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:50.560
That's right, the cat that wins the Jellicle Choice in this case

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:52.880
also happens to be the cat that has shown dissent in the past.

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:56.780
By sending Grizabella away, the cult eliminates one of its malcontents,

00:13:56.780 --> 00:14:00.500
a possible future liability, and silences her permanently.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:03.760
All while making her think that it's her choice and good thing.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:04.640
Gaslighting, anyone?

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:07.000
I mean, how could drifting away into the night in a hot air balloon

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.980
end with anything but eventual painful awkward death?

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:11.400
You don't see ascend,

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.760
we just see see her disappear all by herself

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:16.600
a ritualistic Jellicle sacrifice.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:18.200
And tragically, Victoria's hooked.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.800
Her final versus of Beautiful Ghosts confirm it. Quote,

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:22.800
"And so maybe my home isn't what I had known"

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:24.440
"what I thought it would be"

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:26.800
"But I feel so alive with these phantoms of night"

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.600
"And I know that this life isn't safe, but it's wild"

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:30.560
"And it's free"

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:33.760
"I never knew I'd love this world they've let me into"

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:37.420
I don't know what's worse, the idea this poor cat is being tricked into joining a dangerous cult,

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:40.160
or the slam rhymes that are being used in the song's lyrics.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:43.040
Ugh. Even Virginia Woolf would be cringing in her grave.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.920
Look, I can go on and on.

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:48.360
The Jellicles hit pretty much every aspect of a traditional cult.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.540
At this point I don't even know if this is a theory anymore.

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:53.320
I think maybe this film, and by proxy the musical before it,

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:55.820
was always supposed to be a portrayal of a cult.

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:58.140
And viewers themselves got too wrapped up into it,

00:14:58.140 --> 00:14:59.380
and just didn't notice.

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:03.000
I mean, let's face it, I guess we're ALL a little bit Jellicle now.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:08.220
But hey, that's just a theory! A FILM theory.

